within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.M_MusculoSkeletalSystem.M04A_AntigoutPreparations.M04AA01_Allopurinol;
model Allopurinol_Aksenov2018_PD_kp
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Aksenov_2018 :: kP (production rate of uric acid)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 1.40277777778e-08,      // [kg/s; mg/h × 2.77778e-10]
    Emax = -2.33333333333e-10,  // [kg/s; mg/h × 2.77778e-10]
    EC50 = 0.014,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 140000, Interval = 280),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Allopurinol_Aksenov2018_PD_kp</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Aksenov S et al., <i>Physiological reports 6(5)</i> 2018 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.13614\">doi:10.14814/phy2.13614</a>) — production rate of uric acid [mg/h] against oxypurinol ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       50.5 mg/h     drug-free response (baseline) (k P,0, Q324)
  Emax  =       0.84 mg/h     maximal effect term (R max, Q323)
  EC50  =      14000 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term ([P] 50,PIN, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of oxypurinol per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 1.403e-08   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (14000 ng/mL)  response 1.391e-08
  exposure -> infinity  response 1.379e-08</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Aksenov_2018: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Allopurinol_Aksenov2018_PD_kp;
